# CANONICAL §7.3 / §9 fixture — LEGACY asymmetric Chamfer records (no `referenceFaces`)
# under kernel-hardening WP-F (2026-09-03).
#
# A record written before WP-F carries `distance2` (or `angleDeg`) and no pair. Its
# reference face used to be the ordinal-derived legacy choice, which is exactly what
# mirrored the legs silently (see chamfer_reference_face.ndjson). Under this build
# there is NO legacy rule: the step halts as `needsRepair` with the op-built reason
# `legacyReferenceFace`, `seedEdgeId`, and the edge's two adjacent faces as a
# deliberate tie — the user picks once, Rust CREATES the pair, and the record is
# typed from then on. The rule this file pins is that the halt is the SAME in every
# lane, because the lanes differ only in the `editedFrom` claim and a per-plan gate
# was tried and rejected (REDO and timeline previews omit the claim, so a gated rule
# would have silently replayed the ordinal choice against a permuted face map):
#   * no edit context at all (round 1) — the open / undo / redo / preview lanes;
#   * an UPSTREAM edit (`editedFrom` 1 < step 2, round 2);
#   * an edit OF THE CHAMFER ITSELF (`editedFrom` 2 == step 2, round 3);
#   * the distance-angle form (round 4) shares the reference face and the halt;
#   * an EQUAL-LEG chamfer has no reference face and is untouched by all of this
#     (round 5, the negative control).
# Same box, same edge (e:10, adjacent f:3 -X wall / f:6 top) as
# chamfer_reference_face.ndjson; head never moves (every round is discarded).
